{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4529","id":4734157746,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGi2Dsg","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4529","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4529.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4529.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4529","number":4529,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-R015-T04: capture independent session HTTP and numerical lifecycles","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-R015-T04\nRelated: #426; independent additive follow-up to the merged release15 session fixtures\n\n## Change\n\nAdd a production-browser fixture for three live application sessions across two projects: separate compiler/runtime workers, independent explicit network grants, concurrent held loopback HTTP and managed numerical work, targeted HTTP cancellation, revocation while another application remains selected, survivor completion and revoked-session restart.\n\nThe fixture reuses the existing acceptance runner and actual Studio/compiler/runtime workers. Its fixed endpoint allows one request for each of three fixture tags; no provider credentials are used. Every phase retains observations and a screenshot. Exact clean-source production build identity and served JavaScript hashes are checked before qualification.\n\nA close-RPC acknowledgement is insufficient: the adapter waits for the browser process to exit, requires exit zero and validates the shared launcher's final CSP/browser/teardown record. Cancellation and setup failures remain failures. Revocation waits for both the host registry and actual transport activity to settle.\n\nEven a successful component deliberately returns **blocked / exit 2** for the wider FAIR-SESSION-IO obligation: host-wide numerical admission/fairness and managed WebSocket integration are not demonstrated by this slice.\n\n## Validation and observed blocker\n\n- Exact local commit `c519eb7f961a6e4f912c33524168febb4c10fab2`: **8 focused policy/adapter tests passed**, zero failures/skips, followed by a successful production build.\n- A real runner attempt at that same clean committed build retained **status=failed, componentStatus=unexecuted, browser capability=unavailable**, exit 1. Product session phases did not run.\n- The pinned Playwright 1.63.0 install succeeded. Both the full Chromium and same-revision headless-shell 1243/153.0.8010.12 downloads returned invalid ZIP archives; no browser executable was available. Pins were preserved.\n- The retained failed-run report binds build identity SHA-256 `cba609d7700d5b14e0fffb945a9369eeca6b7a4fb59eb0c5292428451f01a34f`, browser setup diagnostics and artifact digests.\n- Published tree `d55ceac0b6676442b64cf69461292b2e9888870e` exactly matches the locally tested tree; GitHub object publication produced a different commit ID.\n- Required hosted core is the implementation gate. Neither that core nor these policy tests constitute a browser or release-readiness pass.\n\n## Ownership and remaining work\n\nAll eight files are newly added fixture/report/test/documentation paths. Existing release15 leased paths, shared browser launchers, product files, source archives, evidence status and Project/claim refs remain intact.\n\nActual browser execution remains required once the pinned browser is available. Broader R015 also depends on independent document designers, duplicate-instance Hot Reload behavior, product Git/publish capabilities, provider/platform evidence and the trusted release source archive. This PR closes none of those requirements and creates no release.\n\nNo new dependencies or pin changes.\n","created_at":"2026-10-04T11:57:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T11:59:10Z","closed_at":"2026-10-04T11:59:10Z","merged_at":"2026-10-04T11:59:10Z","merge_commit_sha":"47d80eedb06b505013b162e73d5e2ad24082b54e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12524063633,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU59Ms88AAAAC6n4LkQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/labels/size/XXL","name":"size/XXL","color":"E50009","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4529/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4529/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4529/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/statuses/1b41f3b4a6b75eb0dbb9a530ccbfe9cc2867de7c","head":{"label":"wieslawsoltes:codex/p4-release-acceptance","ref":"codex/p4-release-acceptance","sha":"1b41f3b4a6b75eb0dbb9a530ccbfe9cc2867de7c","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.g